    <bpmn:process id="W_W1219" name="W1219. BIR Electronic Invoicing System (EIS) Onboarding &amp; Compliance Readiness" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: BIR mandates EIS compliance for BuildRight entity (based on revenue threshold); or voluntary early adoption decision; or BIR publishes new EIS implementation deadline
Frequency: One-time onboarding per entity; ongoing compliance operations (daily transmission)
Volume: 5 entities to onboard; 33.6M annual POS transactions + ~80,500 AP invoices + ~42,000 AR invoices to be transmitted electronically
Owner: Tax Manager
Participants: Tax Manager, CIO, POS System Administrator, ERP System Administrator, CFO, BIR EIS Helpdesk, External Tax Advisor
Source: workflow W1219 — BIR Electronic Invoicing System (EIS) Onboarding &amp; Compliance Readiness</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1219_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1219_Lane1" name="Tax Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1219_Lane2" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1219_Lane3" name="IT Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1219_Lane4" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1219_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1219_Start6" name="BIR mandates EIS compliance for BuildRight entity (based on revenue threshold); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task7" name="Regulatory assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Regulatory assessment: Tax Manager reviews BIR EIS regulations, revenue regulations, and implementation timelines: (a) confirm which BuildRight entities are mandated and by when, (b) review BIR-prescribed data formats and transmission specifications, (c) assess current ERP/POS system capabilities for EIS compliance, (d) engage external tax advisor for regulatory interpretation, (e) present compliance gap analysis to CFO
Responsible (R): Tax Manager / External Advisor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task8" name="System gap analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System gap analysis: CIO evaluates ERP and POS systems: (a) can current POS generate sales data in BIR-prescribed JSON/XML format?, (b) does ERP support BIR-required sales invoice numbering (sequential, gapless, entity-prefixed)?, (c) can system transmit data to BIR API endpoint (internet connectivity, security certificates)?, (d) identify development or configuration changes needed; estimate IT effort and timeline
Responsible (R): CIO / ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task9" name="Development/configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Development/configuration: IT team implements required changes: (a) configure POS to generate EIS-compliant transaction data: sales invoice number format (entity code + sequential), buyer TIN (for B2B transactions), line-item detail (item description, quantity, unit price, VAT amount), payment method, (b) build or configure EIS transmission module: API integration with BIR EIS endpoint, JSON/XML data formatting, digital certificate authentication, retry logic for failed transmissions, (c) configure monitoring dashboard: transmission success rate, failed transmissions, pending queue, (d) update CAS registration with BIR to reflect EIS capability
Responsible (R): IT Team / ERP Vendor
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task10" name="Testing and certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Testing and certification: (a) IT team conducts end-to-end testing using BIR EIS test environment (sandbox): generate sample transactions from POS, transmit to BIS test endpoint, verify BIR acknowledgment receipt; (b) test edge cases: offline POS transactions (W5G) — how are offline transactions transmitted upon reconnection?, void transactions, return transactions, consignment sales, (c) Tax Manager verifies transaction data accuracy and completeness per BIR requirements, (d) submit test results to BIR for certification (if required by applicable revenue regulation)
Responsible (R): IT Team / Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task11" name="CAS permit update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: CAS permit update: Tax Manager submits updated CAS application to BIR: (a) updated system description including EIS capability, (b) sample printouts and electronic data format, (c) system process flow documentation, (d) BIR may conduct system demonstration or inspection per W216; obtain updated CAS permit with EIS endorsement
Responsible (R): Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–4 weeks (BIR processing)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task12" name="Go-live">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Go-live: (a) IT activates EIS transmission for first entity (BuildRight Depot, Inc. — largest transaction volume); (b) initial parallel run: transmit data to BIR while maintaining manual backup per W540; (c) monitor transmission success rate for first 2 weeks — target ≥ 99.5%; (d) resolve any transmission failures immediately (failed transmissions must be retransmitted within BIR-prescribed timeframe); (e) once stable for first entity: activate remaining 4 entities in sequence
Responsible (R): IT Team / Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–4 weeks per entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task13" name="Staff training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Staff training: (a) Tax Accountant trained on EIS compliance monitoring and exception handling, (b) IT Helpdesk trained on troubleshooting transmission failures, (c) Store Managers informed of any POS workflow changes (e.g., mandatory customer TIN capture for B2B transactions, updated receipt format with EIS reference number), (d) AR team trained on updated sales invoice requirements for trade/corporate accounts
Responsible (R): Tax Manager / CIO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1219_Task14" name="Ongoing compliance operations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Ongoing compliance operations: (a) daily: system transmits sales transaction data to BIR EIS endpoint within prescribed timeframe, (b) daily: IT monitors transmission dashboard — resolves any failures within same business day, (c) monthly: Tax Accountant reconciles EIS-transmitted data vs. ERP sales records vs. VAT return (W90) — all three must match, (d) quarterly: Tax Manager reviews BIR EIS bulletins for format or specification changes; coordinate IT updates as needed per W657
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / IT Helpdesk
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1219_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1219_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1219_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1219_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-309 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Change Management (PA-22.3).)
Owner: Tax Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1219_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1219_Annotation16" targetRef="W1219_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1219_Flow18" sourceRef="W1219_Start6" targetRef="W1219_Task7" />
